AB  - The Electronic Privacy Information Center (EPIC) submits comments to the Department of Justice (DOJ) and Department of Homeland Security (DHS) regarding the use of facial recognition, biometric, and predictive algorithm technologies by law enforcement. EPIC expresses concern about the lack of transparency, accountability, and oversight in the deployment of these technologies, emphasizing the need for stronger safeguards to protect privacy, civil rights, and civil liberties. EPIC recommends prohibiting mass surveillance, protecting constitutional rights, ensuring non-discrimination, and requiring thorough evaluations before deploying new surveillance technologies. The comments also address specific technologies like facial recognition, predictive policing, social media surveillance, and DNA analysis, advocating for adherence to key principles that promote public trust and fairness.
