AB  - This chapter provides generalization of existing approaches to the definition of design and determinants of the smart awareness development among the youth of Ukraine, and also describes the current state of perception of the Smart City Concept. The authors conducted a survey of students of higher education institutions in Dnipro, Ukraine regarding their perception of the Smart City Concept (n = 200 subjects). Respondents most often use the following services of a "smart" city: electronic tickets, tracking the transport schedules, electronic administration services, eHealth system, and information technologies in educational institutions. It has been proved that management in a smart city takes place through the synergy of everyone who lives and works in this city - the classic triad "government - business - community." The Smart City provides comfortable living conditions for inhabitants and simplified technologies for using services offered by city institutions. In Ukraine, such cooperation is built in the following areas: city security (safe city), medicine (e-health), education (smart education), transportation system (smart mobility), electric power supply (smart energy) and the formation of the city as a creative center (creative hubs). The chapter also considers the influence of military operations as an attractor of expanding the network of e-services in Ukraine. Social risks and limitations for spreading smart awareness and smart culture are analyzed. The authors pay special attention to the practical expertise of building smart infrastructure in Ukrainian cities, in particular, to the main achievements as well as obstacles that stand in the way of the widespread smart technologies introduction into the city's life support system. © 2023 Nova Science Publishers, Inc. All rights reserved.
